% Test cases for the Vitamin D Assay Testing policy (vitamin_d.le): synthetic
% claims, each stating only what its record shows, and each read under all
% six A/B MAC jurisdictions at once. The queries: whether the claim is
% reasonable and necessary in its own jurisdiction (the scenario's "the
% jurisdiction of claim 1 is ..."), and in which jurisdictions it would be.
% No "pay" query: dmepos.le's payable rule asks for a delivery and a proof
% of delivery, which a laboratory test has none of (vitamin_d.le, header).

the target language is: prolog.

the knowledge base vitamin d cases includes these resources:
    vitamin_d.

the knowledge base vitamin d cases includes:

query rn is:
    which claim is reasonable and necessary.

query rn_in is:
    which claim is reasonable and necessary in which jurisdiction.

% Vitamin D deficiency (E55.9), a code every article lists: covered in all
% six jurisdictions.
scenario deficiency_everywhere is:
    claim 1 is for the vitamin D assay.
    the HCPCS code of the vitamin D assay is "82306".
    the vitamin D assay is furnished to Ann.
    the date of service of claim 1 is 2026-06-01.
    the jurisdiction of claim 1 is cgs.
    the diagnosis code of Ann is "E55.9".
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary"].
    rn_in expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary in first coast", "claim 1 is reasonable and necessary in cgs", "claim 1 is reasonable and necessary in wps", "claim 1 is reasonable and necessary in noridian", "claim 1 is reasonable and necessary in wellpoint", "claim 1 is reasonable and necessary in palmetto"].

% Psoriasis vulgaris (L40.0): in the tables of First Coast, WPS, Noridian
% and Wellpoint, not in those of CGS (the jurisdiction) or Palmetto.
scenario psoriasis_by_jurisdiction is:
    claim 1 is for the vitamin D assay.
    the HCPCS code of the vitamin D assay is "82306".
    the vitamin D assay is furnished to Ben.
    the date of service of claim 1 is 2026-06-01.
    the jurisdiction of claim 1 is cgs.
    the diagnosis code of Ben is "L40.0".
    rn expects answers [].
    rn_in expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary in first coast", "claim 1 is reasonable and necessary in wps", "claim 1 is reasonable and necessary in noridian", "claim 1 is reasonable and necessary in wellpoint"].

