scenario dihydroxy_hypercalcemia is:
    claim 1 is for the dihydroxy assay.
    the HCPCS code of the dihydroxy assay is "82652".
    the dihydroxy assay is furnished to Eve.
    the date of service of claim 1 is 2026-06-01.
    the jurisdiction of claim 1 is cgs.
    the diagnosis code of Eve is "E83.52".
    rn expects answers [].
    rn_in expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary in noridian", "claim 1 is reasonable and necessary in wellpoint", "claim 1 is reasonable and necessary in palmetto"].

% A general adult examination (Z00.00): screening, covered nowhere — not
% even in CGS, whose LCD names the documented low exposure to sunlight.
scenario screening_examination is:
    claim 1 is for the vitamin D assay.
    the HCPCS code of the vitamin D assay is "82306".
    the vitamin D assay is furnished to Fay.
    the date of service of claim 1 is 2026-06-01.
    the jurisdiction of claim 1 is palmetto.
    the diagnosis code of Fay is "Z00.00".
    the medical record of Fay documents low exposure to sunlight.
    rn expects answers [].
    rn_in expects answers [].

% Low exposure to sunlight documented for a housebound beneficiary (Z74.09,
% in no table): an indication CGS's LCD lists in prose, and only CGS's.
scenario sunlight_cgs is:
    claim 1 is for the vitamin D assay.
    the HCPCS code of the vitamin D assay is "82306".
    the vitamin D assay is furnished to Gus.
    the date of service of claim 1 is 2026-06-01.
    the jurisdiction of claim 1 is cgs.
    the diagnosis code of Gus is "Z74.09".
    the medical record of Gus documents low exposure to sunlight.
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary"].
    rn_in expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary in cgs"].

% A pregnancy (supervision of normal pregnancy, Z34.90, in no table):
