    the jurisdiction of claim 1 is palmetto.
    the diagnosis code of Ida is "Z34.90".
    the medical record of Ida documents pregnancy.
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary"].
    rn_in expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary in palmetto"].

% A fourth test in the year for a deficiency, in First Coast: more than
% three tests per year. WPS allows four for a deficiency; the others set
% no number.
scenario fourth_test_first_coast is:
    claim 1 is for the vitamin D assay.
    the HCPCS code of the vitamin D assay is "82306".
    the vitamin D assay is furnished to Jon.
    the date of service of claim 1 is 2026-06-01.
    the jurisdiction of claim 1 is first coast.
    the diagnosis code of Jon is "E55.9".
    Jon had a vitamin D test on 2026-01-15.
    Jon had a vitamin D test on 2026-03-01.
    Jon had a vitamin D test on 2026-04-20.
    rn expects answers [].
    rn_in expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary in cgs", "claim 1 is reasonable and necessary in wps", "claim 1 is reasonable and necessary in noridian", "claim 1 is reasonable and necessary in wellpoint", "claim 1 is reasonable and necessary in palmetto"].

% A fifth test in the year for a deficiency, in WPS: beyond its four per
% year (and First Coast's three).
scenario fifth_test_wps is:
    claim 1 is for the vitamin D assay.
    the HCPCS code of the vitamin D assay is "82306".
    the vitamin D assay is furnished to Lou.
    the date of service of claim 1 is 2026-06-01.
    the jurisdiction of claim 1 is wps.
    the diagnosis code of Lou is "E55.9".
    Lou had a vitamin D test on 2025-07-01.
    Lou had a vitamin D test on 2026-01-15.
    Lou had a vitamin D test on 2026-03-01.
    Lou had a vitamin D test on 2026-04-20.
    rn expects answers [].
    rn_in expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary in cgs", "claim 1 is reasonable and necessary in noridian", "claim 1 is reasonable and necessary in wellpoint", "claim 1 is reasonable and necessary in palmetto"].

% A second test in the year for osteoporosis (M81.0), in WPS: once a year
% for a condition other than a deficiency. Noridian and Wellpoint cover
% osteoporosis only with one of their five conditions documented; First
% Coast, CGS and Palmetto cover it.
scenario second_test_osteoporosis_wps is:
    claim 1 is for the vitamin D assay.
    the HCPCS code of the vitamin D assay is "82306".
    the vitamin D assay is furnished to Kim.
    the date of service of claim 1 is 2026-06-01.
    the jurisdiction of claim 1 is wps.
    the diagnosis code of Kim is "M81.0".
    Kim had a vitamin D test on 2026-02-01.
    rn expects answers [].
    rn_in expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary in first coast", "claim 1 is reasonable and necessary in cgs", "claim 1 is reasonable and necessary in palmetto"].

% Osteoporosis in Noridian with a history of fragility fractures: condition
% ii of its LCD, met; a first test, covered everywhere.
scenario osteoporosis_fracture_history_noridian is:
    claim 1 is for the vitamin D assay.
    the HCPCS code of the vitamin D assay is "82306".
    the vitamin D assay is furnished to Pat.
    the date of service of claim 1 is 2026-06-01.
    the jurisdiction of claim 1 is noridian.
    the diagnosis code of Pat is "M81.0".
    the medical record of Pat documents history of fragility fractures.
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary"].
    rn_in expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary in first coast", "claim 1 is reasonable and necessary in cgs", "claim 1 is reasonable and necessary in wps", "claim 1 is reasonable and necessary in noridian", "claim 1 is reasonable and necessary in wellpoint", "claim 1 is reasonable and necessary in palmetto"].

% A second level on the same day, in First Coast: one per 24 hour period
% (First Coast, WPS); the others state no daily limit.
scenario same_day_repeat is:
    claim 1 is for the vitamin D assay.
    the HCPCS code of the vitamin D assay is "82306".
    the vitamin D assay is furnished to Max.
    the date of service of claim 1 is 2026-06-01.
    the jurisdiction of claim 1 is first coast.
    the diagnosis code of Max is "E55.9".
    Max had a vitamin D test on 2026-06-01.
    rn expects answers [].
    rn_in expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary in cgs", "claim 1 is reasonable and necessary in noridian", "claim 1 is reasonable and necessary in wellpoint", "claim 1 is reasonable and necessary in palmetto"].

% Supplemented to normal levels, a second test in the year, in CGS: annual
% testing thereafter (CGS, Palmetto, First Coast); WPS's four a year for a
% deficiency, and Noridian's and Wellpoint's repeat rule, still allow it.
scenario supplemented_second_test_cgs is:
    claim 1 is for the vitamin D assay.
    the HCPCS code of the vitamin D assay is "82306".
    the vitamin D assay is furnished to Ned.
    the date of service of claim 1 is 2026-06-01.
    the jurisdiction of claim 1 is cgs.
    the diagnosis code of Ned is "E55.9".
    Ned has been supplemented to normal vitamin D levels.
    Ned had a vitamin D test on 2026-02-01.
    rn expects answers [].
    rn_in expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary in wps", "claim 1 is reasonable and necessary in noridian", "claim 1 is reasonable and necessary in wellpoint"].

% Supplemented to normal levels, the annual test (the last one fifteen
% months ago), in Palmetto, with nothing in the record supporting the need
% for it: Palmetto alone asks for that.
scenario annual_test_undocumented_palmetto is:
    claim 1 is for the vitamin D assay.
    the HCPCS code of the vitamin D assay is "82306".
    the vitamin D assay is furnished to Oli.
    the date of service of claim 1 is 2026-06-01.
    the jurisdiction of claim 1 is palmetto.
    the diagnosis code of Oli is "E55.9".
    Oli has been supplemented to normal vitamin D levels.
    Oli had a vitamin D test on 2025-03-01.
    rn expects answers [].
    rn_in expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary in first coast", "claim 1 is reasonable and necessary in cgs", "claim 1 is reasonable and necessary in wps", "claim 1 is reasonable and necessary in noridian", "claim 1 is reasonable and necessary in wellpoint"].

% A repeat test of a clinically stable beneficiary whose last level was 35
% ng/ml, in Wellpoint: claim 1 with nothing on its necessity, claim 2 with
% the record clearly indicating it. Noridian reads the same; the other four
% set no such condition.
scenario stable_normal_repeat_wellpoint is:
    claim 1 is for the vitamin D assay.
    claim 2 is for the vitamin D assay.
    the HCPCS code of the vitamin D assay is "82306".
    the vitamin D assay is furnished to Quin.
    the date of service of claim 1 is 2026-06-01.
    the date of service of claim 2 is 2026-06-01.
    the jurisdiction of claim 1 is wellpoint.
    the jurisdiction of claim 2 is wellpoint.
    the diagnosis code of Quin is "E55.9".
    Quin had a vitamin D test on 2026-02-15.
    the most recent vitamin D level of Quin is 35 ng per ml.
    Quin is clinically stable.
    the record clearly indicates the necessity of the test of claim 2.
    rn expects answers ["claim 2 is reasonable and necessary"].
    rn_in expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary in first coast", "claim 1 is reasonable and necessary in cgs", "claim 1 is reasonable and necessary in wps", "claim 1 is reasonable and necessary in palmetto", "claim 2 is reasonable and necessary in first coast", "claim 2 is reasonable and necessary in cgs", "claim 2 is reasonable and necessary in wps", "claim 2 is reasonable and necessary in noridian", "claim 2 is reasonable and necessary in wellpoint", "claim 2 is reasonable and necessary in palmetto"].
